Additional permission under GNU AGPL version 3 section 7
========================================================

Stud is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
or later; the full text is in LICENSE. This file adds a permission on top
of it. It only ever grants: if you never rely on it, Stud is plain AGPLv3
to you, unchanged.


The permission
--------------

  As an additional permission under section 7 of the GNU Affero General
  Public License version 3, the copyright holders of Stud give you
  permission to link or combine Stud with the Roblox Engine, and to
  convey the resulting work.

  "The Roblox Engine" means the software contained in the Roblox
  application packages published by Roblox Corporation, among them the
  Roblox player and Roblox Studio, and any library loaded from them:
  software under terms incompatible with the GNU Affero General Public
  License, which Stud neither includes nor distributes, and which is
  downloaded from Roblox Corporation's own servers onto the machine of
  the person running Stud.

  You must still comply with the GNU Affero General Public License in
  all respects for all of the code used other than the Roblox Engine.

  If you modify Stud, you may extend this permission to your version,
  but you are not obliged to. If you do not wish to, delete this
  statement from your version.


Why it exists
-------------

Stud starts the Roblox client and works alongside it: it writes the
client's settings and content files, and reads its output. Whether that
makes a combined work whose distribution the AGPL would forbid is the old
question about combining with proprietary code, and it is a question
nobody involved should have to spend time on.

In Stud's case there is a good argument that it never arises. The client
runs as a process of its own under Rosemary, with none of Stud's code
loaded into it. Stud does not ship the client or mirror it: it is
downloaded from Roblox's own servers onto the machine of the person
running Stud, so whatever combination happens, happens there and is
never conveyed to anyone. Every binary Stud does redistribute, Rosemary
among them, ships with its own licence and notice.

This permission is here so that argument does not have to be made. A
distribution packaging Stud, and anyone building on it, can rely on the
grant instead of on a reading.
